    "body": "### Problem\n\nIf you have a two windows open inside neovim side by side. One of which is :terminal. If you resize your terminal emulator (kitty in my case) so much that :terminal becomes too small and gets pushed off screen, neovim crashes.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\nnvim --clean\n# Open a new vertically split window\n<C-W>v\n# Focus the new window\n<C-l>\n# Open a terminal\n:terminal\n\nNow change the width of the terminal emulator\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/033d6c5b-565e-408d-babe-c4d4881a0ce3\n\n[backtrace.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32095565/backtrace.txt)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNot crash\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.13.0-dev-1596+g28ff47b8a4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux 7.2.4-arch1-2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.48.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\npacman neovim or AUR neovim-nightly. Both have the same issue",
